From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 21:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: reset PPE VP state on recovery

The ath12k datapath object survives firmware recovery even though its bank
profiles and direct-switch node are destroyed and recreated.
Reinitializing the PPE descriptor pool without clearing the VP allocation
bitmaps leaves
profiles marked busy with stale reference counts.  Repeated recoveries can
therefore exhaust the profile table or reuse a bank from the previous
datapath instance.

Reset both allocation maps and all profile reference counts when the new
direct-switch descriptor pool is initialized.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
@@ -169,10 +169,13 @@ static int ath12k_ppe_ds_tx_desc_init(st
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&ppe->tx_desc_free_list);
 	spin_lock_init(&ppe->tx_desc_lock);
 	spin_lock_init(&ppe->vp_lock);
+	ppe->vp_profile_map = 0;
+	ppe->search_idx_map = 0;
 	for (i = 0; i < ATH12K_PPE_DS_VP_PROFILES; i++) {
 		ppe->vp_profiles[i].vp = -1;
 		ppe->vp_profiles[i].search_idx = -1;
 		ppe->vp_profiles[i].bank_id = DP_INVALID_BANK_ID;
+		ppe->vp_profiles[i].refcount = 0;
 	}
 
 	ppe->tx_desc_pages = kcalloc(DP_PPE_DS_TX_SPT_PAGES,
